window.WIKI_ENTRY={"id": "concept-023", "name_zh": "心理时间", "name_en": "psychological time", "tagline": "赛斯说的心理时间不是「快乐就觉得短」那种主观快慢，而是内我本来的时间感——他把它排作你的第二内在感官，也是所有内在资料必须经过的那条通道。", "explanation": "赛斯把心理时间定位在内我一侧：它属于心智，是他口中「第二内在感官」的别名，是一条来回内在与外在世界的天然通道。它与钟表时间不是对立而是包裹——物理时间是披在心理时间外面的一件晚礼服，是它最忠实的复制品；钟表时间则是意识自我基于恐惧发明出来的切分法，切得越细，心理时间越无法自由流动。他说心理时间是你们层面上最小的公分母：许多障碍在这里消失，是最接近无时间的经验。梦是这条论证的第一块证据——梦里过两天身体不会老两岁，因为梦只存在于心理时间的架构里；他更进一步说，整个地球早期就运作在这样一个梦世界中。赛斯称它为其他所有内在资料必经的通道，机制在于「伪装在这里松开」：最大程度运用心理时间时，人格在很大程度上绕过物质法则，也绕过那些让物质架构负荷过重的化学反应。他要的是可随时切回来的两用能力，而不是逃避排程：从十五二十分钟开始、固定时间、心中有一件特定的事、实验前以湿布敷眼；最常见的失败是用力，他反复提醒「这会造成压缩，我们要的是扩展」，并数次替珍与罗缩短或暂停练习。他给的结果是短时间内大量充电、减少对睡眠的需求、在物质世界里不再被催赶；往深处说，它让死亡的经验不那么可怕，让你能感知现在就存在的更大实相与另一个系统中的自己。这一页的另一半价值在记录：1964 年起珍与罗真的每天练习并逐条留档，罗甚至为每个经验画素描——他记下震颤与「歌唱」般的觉受如何被任何声音增强，珍记下看清老家街道、把感知投进病房并与当事人核对。这些括号里的记录，是赛斯这套说法唯一的现场证词。", "definitions": [{"zh": "所谓的心理时间属于内我，也就是说属于心智。不过它是一个连结物，是一种内在感官的一部分，为了方便起见我们将称之为第二内在感官。", "en": "Psychological time so-called belongs to the inner self, that is to the mind. It is however a connective, a portion of one of the inner senses, which we will call for convenience the second inner sense.", "source": "Session 23"}, {"zh": "基本上，意识本身就是一种障碍，任何有意识的东西都会在某种程度上经历时间。这个程度对你们来说可能是如此的轻微，以至于觉得它根本就不存在。自我意识呈现出更大的障碍，因此时间感也更强。从你们的观点来看，心理时间是最小的公分母。也就是说，许多的障碍不见了。在你们的层面上，心理时间代表着你们最接近没有时间的经验。", "en": "Now basically, consciousness itself is a type of barrier, and anything that has consciousness experiences time to some degree. This degree may be so slight that to you it would not seem to exist at all. Self-consciousness presents a larger barrier, therefore the sense of time is greater. Psychological time is the lowest common denominator, so to speak, from your viewpoint. That is, many of the barriers disappear. Psychological time represents on your plane the closest you can come to the experience of timelessness as far as your physical laws are concerned.", "source": "Session 35"}, {"zh": "外在物理时间是一个完全的伪装，在你们层面基本上并非必要；但你们让它变得好像非要不可，因为你们拒绝承认内我是整个人格的一部分，所以无法在你们层面上充分利用心理时间的优点。心理时间，就像我说过的，是一条天然通道，一种内在感官的一部分，作用是来回内在世界与外在世界的一条捷径。你们并没有这样利用它。", "en": "Outer physical time is a complete camouflage, unnecessary basically on your plane; but you have made it seem necessary because of your refusal to admit the inner self as part of your whole personality, and therefore you have not been able to utilize psychological time to its fullest advantage on your plane. Psychological time as I have said is a natural pathway, part of an inner sense, that was meant as an easy access from the inner to the outer world and back again. You do not use it as such.", "source": "Session 23"}, {"zh": "心理时间的确是唯一的传导媒介或框架，在那框架中，内我可以进行探索。", "en": "Psychological time is indeed the only medium, or framework, within which exploration of the inner self can be carried on.", "source": "Session 84"}, {"zh": "心理时间是一种对所有意识的存在都有利的气候或环境。", "en": "Psychological time is a sort of climate or environment conducive to the existence of all consciousness.", "source": "Session 43"}], "blocks": [{"id": "B01", "title": "它是什么：属于内我的时间感，也就是你的第二内在感官", "note": "时间是你们最明显的伪装之一，研究时间将会用一种相当直接的方式，带领你从伪装的肉身自己，来到你忽略的内我¹。所谓的心理时间属于内我，也就是说属于心智——它是一个连结物，是一种内在感官的一部分，为了方便起见赛斯将称之为第二内在感官²；它是一条天然通道，作用是来回内在世界与外在世界的一条捷径³。不过要留意：第二种内在感官「就像是你们的时间感」，这只是个方便的说法，别把两者过度仔细比较⁴。\n\n那它在时间谱系里站在哪？基本上，意识本身就是一种障碍，自我意识这个障碍更大，所以时间感也更强；而心理时间是最小的公分母——许多障碍在这里不见了，它代表着你们最接近没有时间的经验⁵。也正因为如此，它是其他所有内在资料必经的通道⁶；到后面这句话被推到顶：心理时间的确是唯一的传导媒介或框架，在那框架中，内我可以进行探索⁷。\n\n最后说范围：大部分的实相与你们想像的空间一点关系都没有，它们在类似心理时间的东西里有自己的成长和存在，而心理时间是一种对所有意识的存在都有利的气候或环境⁸。\n\n所以这一页最好当成一张地图来读，而不是当成一种技巧来读。", "src": "早期课第1册第 23、24、35 节；早期课第2册第 43、84 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": "q-concept-023-e0001", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第23节"}, {"n": 2, "id": "q-concept-023-e0002", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第23节"}, {"n": 3, "id": "q-concept-023-e0003", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第23节"}, {"n": 4, "id": "q-concept-023-e0006", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第24节"}, {"n": 5, "id": "q-concept-023-e0031", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第35节"}, {"n": 6, "id": "q-concept-023-e0033", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第35节"}, {"n": 7, "id": "q-concept-023-e0145", "label": "早期课第2册 · 第84节"}, {"n": 8, "id": "q-concept-023-e0042", "label": "早期课第2册 · 第43节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-023-e0001", "zh": "时间是你们最明显的伪装之一，研究时间将会用一种相当直接的方式，带领你从伪装的肉身自己，来到你忽略的内我。甚至现在你们的心理学家也谈到用来设定时钟的物理时间，以及心理时间之间的差异。", "en": "Time is one of your most obvious camouflages, and the study of time will lead you in a fairly direct manner from the camouflaged physical self to the inner self, which you ignore. Even now your psychologists speak of the difference between physical time, by which you set your clocks, and psychological time.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第23节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "23", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0002", "zh": "所谓的心理时间属于内我，也就是说属于心智。不过它是一个连结物，是一种内在感官的一部分，为了方便起见我们将称之为第二内在感官。", "en": "Psychological time so-called belongs to the inner self, that is to the mind. It is however a connective, a portion of one of the inner senses, which we will call for convenience the second inner sense.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第23节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "23", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0003", "zh": "外在物理时间是一个完全的伪装，在你们层面基本上并非必要；但你们让它变得好像非要不可，因为你们拒绝承认内我是整个人格的一部分，所以无法在你们层面上充分利用心理时间的优点。心理时间，就像我说过的，是一条天然通道，一种内在感官的一部分，作用是来回内在世界与外在世界的一条捷径。你们并没有这样利用它。", "en": "Outer physical time is a complete camouflage, unnecessary basically on your plane; but you have made it seem necessary because of your refusal to admit the inner self as part of your whole personality, and therefore you have not been able to utilize psychological time to its fullest advantage on your plane. Psychological time as I have said is a natural pathway, part of an inner sense, that was meant as an easy access from the inner to the outer world and back again. You do not use it as such.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第23节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "23", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0006", "zh": "这与一种内在感官，第二种内在感官，有密切的关系，你们必须试着根据心理时间，调换你们的内在感官。你可以看出我们双方有许多障碍难行，因为尝试从外在资料的角度，让你们了解内在资料是困难重重的，这两者分得那么开，但其实，又如此紧密相连。比方说，我告诉你们，第二种内在感官就像是你们的时间感，虽然这的确让你们对这第二种感官是怎么一回事有一定的了解或是感觉，但它还是令人困惑，我知道，因为你们很容易过度仔细比较这两者。", "en": "This is closely related to one of the inner senses, the second inner sense, and it is upon psychological time that you must try to transpose your inner visions. You can see how handicapped we both are because of the difficulties involved in trying to make you understand inner data in terms of outer data, when the two are so apart, really, even while they are so closely connected. For instance, when I tell you that the second sense is like your sense of time, while this does give you a certain understanding or feeling of what this second sense is like, nevertheless it also is confusing, I know, because you are apt to compare the two too closely.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第24节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "24", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-023-e0031", "zh": "基本上，意识本身就是一种障碍，任何有意识的东西都会在某种程度上经历时间。这个程度对你们来说可能是如此的轻微，以至于觉得它根本就不存在。自我意识呈现出更大的障碍，因此时间感也更强。从你们的观点来看，心理时间是最小的公分母。也就是说，许多的障碍不见了。在你们的层面上，心理时间代表着你们最接近没有时间的经验。", "en": "Now basically, consciousness itself is a type of barrier, and anything that has consciousness experiences time to some degree. This degree may be so slight that to you it would not seem to exist at all. Self-consciousness presents a larger barrier, therefore the sense of time is greater. Psychological time is the lowest common denominator, so to speak, from your viewpoint. That is, many of the barriers disappear. Psychological time represents on your plane the closest you can come to the experience of timelessness as far as your physical laws are concerned.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第35节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "35", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0033", "zh": "今天晚上，我不想再探讨其他内在感官的资料了，因为现在开始说第四种内在感官为时已晚。要像我说过的那样，尝试使用心理时间。这是非常有价值的，因为在你们的这个阶段，它是其他所有内在资料必经的通道。", "en": "I do not want to go into other inner sense material this evening as it is too late to begin on the fourth inner sense. Try and use psychological time as I have told you. This is extremely valuable, for it is the channel through which all other inner data must come at your particular stage.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第35节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "35", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-023-e0042", "zh": "大部分的实相与你们想像的空间一点关系都没有。大部分的实相在类似我们称之为心理时间之内有它们自己的成长和存在，而这就像你们以为的那样完全独立于空间之外。心理时间是一种对所有意识的存在都有利的气候或环境。", "en": "Most realities have absolutely nothing to do with space as you imagine it. Most realities have their growth and existence in something closely akin to what we have called psychological time, and this is completely independent of space as you conceive it to be. Psychological time is a sort of climate or environment conducive to the existence of all consciousness.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第43节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "43", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0145", "zh": "心理时间的确是唯一的传导媒介或框架，在那框架中，内我可以进行探索。此外，随着秋天的到来，你们两个应该会发现，你们自己进入了你们实验的活跃范围里。季节的转换永远会提升心灵能量更多的爆发，稍后我会针对这一点来进行讨论，不过，其实这个心灵能量爆发的增加，其主要作用是为了转换季节。", "en": "Psychological time is indeed the only medium, or framework, within which exploration of the inner self can be carried on. Again, you should both find yourselves coming within a sphere of activity in your experiments, with the coming of autumn. For reasons that I will discuss later, the shift of seasons always gives rise to added bursts of psychic energy, though indeed the added bursts of psychic energy are in main responsible for the shift of seasons.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第84节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "84", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B02", "title": "它和钟表时间：披在外面的那件晚礼服", "note": "赛斯并不要求你不看钟。物理时间——季节、潮汐、昼夜——在他眼里「就像是一件令人赏心悦目、飘逸的晚礼服，披在心理时间上面」，是心理时间最忠实的一个复制品¹。心理时间融入物理时间本来几乎没有困难，但把一天切割成那么多钟表时间片断，心理时间就无法不受阻碍或自由地流动，而钟表时间这个概念，是意识自我基于恐惧的前提发明出来的²。\n\n从内我那一侧看：对内在自我而言，钟表时间并不存在，因为「没有障碍，就没有时间」，内在自我意识到的障碍很少³。所以把心理时间用起来，你会看到钟表时间和你一度以为的内在时间一样如梦似幻，并且发现「所有的时间都是同一个时间，所有的划分都是幻相」⁴。\n\n它能带来什么？心理时间几乎可以让你们拥有「广阔的现在」的自由，某程度上帮助你们看穿过去与未来之间的墙⁵；经由自己的心理时间实验，你们会直接体验到「基本上没有过去、现在和未来」⁶。在赛斯那一侧，时间不是钟点而是强度——「我们是按照经验的强度来感受『时间』」，一个有着自己的高峰与低谷的心理时间⁷；当时间仿佛加快或减慢，它与情绪性感受有些相似，却在重要的地方极为不同⁸。\n\n罗记过比尔的一件事：他习惯把时间切碎、以分钟计算，于是白天永远不够用；而类似心理时间的时间概念，会让他有足够的时间做他想做的所有事⁹。", "src": "早期课第1册第 24、36、41 节；早期课第2册第 54 节；灵魂永生第 515 节；早期课第4册第 184 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": "q-concept-023-e0015", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第24节"}, {"n": 2, "id": "q-concept-023-e0010", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第24节"}, {"n": 3, "id": "q-concept-023-e0035", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第36节"}, {"n": 4, "id": "q-concept-023-e0017", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第24节"}, {"n": 5, "id": "q-concept-023-e0040", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第41节"}, {"n": 6, "id": "q-concept-023-e0090", "label": "早期课第2册 · 第54节"}, {"n": 7, "id": "q-concept-023-e0327", "label": "灵魂永生 · 第515节"}, {"n": 8, "id": "q-concept-023-e0328", "label": "灵魂永生 · 第515节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-023-e0010", "zh": "心理时间融入物理时间几乎没有困难。原先，这让人在很多方面能够相当轻易地活在内在与外在世界里。心理时间可以调换成物理时间，但如果把一天切割成那么多钟表时间片断，心理时间就无法不受阻碍或自由地流动。钟表时间概念是人的意识自我基于恐惧的前提，为了很多不同的理由而发明出来的。", "en": "Psychological time fits into physical time with little trouble. Originally this enabled man in many ways to live in the inner and the outer world with relative ease. Psychological time can be transposed onto physical time, but psychological time cannot flow unhampered or with any freedom through days chopped up into so many clock divisions. The clock time idea was invented by the conscious ego of man for many various reasons, with fear in the foreground.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第24节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "24", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0015", "zh": "你们的物理时间，像是季节或潮汐，白天及黑夜，对我来说是你们最讨人喜欢的伪装之一，如果鲁柏原谅我笨拙的试图诗情画意，那我会说，物理时间就像是一件令人赏心悦目、飘逸的晚礼服，披在心理时间上面，具有许多不同的颜色、质料和图案。它是心理时间最忠实的一个复制品，并且是你们最真实的伪装之一。", "en": "Your physical time of seasons and tides, and night and day, is to me one of your most delightful camouflages, and if Ruburt will excuse my clumsy attempt at being poetical, I will say that physical time is like a delightful flowing gown that clothes psychological time with many different colors and materials and designs. It is a most faithful reproduction of psychological time, and one of your truest camouflages.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第24节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "24", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0017", "zh": "心理时间让“持续时间”更久。你会发现在这里还有别的东西。从心理时间架构内，你会看到钟表时间和你一度以为的内在时间一样，如梦似幻、稍纵即逝。你会发现内在时间和你一度认为的外在时间一样真实。你会发现你的全我们（whole selves）在其他的世界里，同时向内和向外窥视，发现所有的时间都是同一个时间，所有的划分都是幻相。", "en": "Psychological time adds duration. You will find something else here. From the framework of psychological time you will see that clock time is as dreamlike and fleeting as you once thought inner time was. And you will discover that inner time is as much a reality as you once thought outer time was. You will discover your whole selves in other worlds, peeping inward and outward at the same time, and finding that all time is one time, and that all divisions are illusion.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第24节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "24", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-023-e0035", "zh": "你们知道，你们的钟表时间是伪装，对内在自我而言，钟表时间并不存在。这一点你们的确不应该觉得奇怪，因为你们知道，你们现在的人格甚至可以通过使用心理时间，而在一定程度上逃离钟表时间。我曾经说过，没有障碍，就没有时间。内在自我意识到的障碍很少，因此被时间束缚的程度不像外在自我那么大。", "en": "Your clock time as you know is camouflage, and does not exist as far as the inner ego is concerned. This certainly should not be strange to you, since you know that even your present personalities can to some extent escape from clock time through the use of psychological time. I have said that there is no time without barriers. The inner ego is aware of fewer barriers and therefore is not bound by time to the degree that the outer ego is bound.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第36节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "36", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0040", "zh": "这个资料的某些部分，需要一定的时间来适应，但我想现在就把这部分提供给你们；也许你们会看到，运用心理时间对于你们有多么重要。心理时间几乎可以让你们拥有广阔的现在的自由。有关这方面，我后面还会说更多，但是你们心理时间的经验，某程度上，将会帮助你们看穿过去与未来之间的墙。我知道，由于你们自己层面之中情境的关系，你们对于“没有开始也没有结束”这句话，几乎无法理解，而这一部分也已经被知道有好几世纪了。你们自己爱因斯坦的理论，将会助上一臂之力，使这种观念在科学上占有重要地位。", "en": "Some of this material will take some getting used to but I wanted to give it to you now; and perhaps you will see how important the use of psychological time can be to you. It comes very close to allowing you the freedom of the spacious present. There is more I will say later along these lines, but your experience with psychological time will to some degree help you to see through the walls of past and future. I realize you will find the statement, there is no beginning or end, almost incomprehensible, because of your own situation on your own plane, and yet this has been known for centuries; and your own Einstein’s theories will help to give the idea scientific respectability.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第41节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "41", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0090", "zh": "你们自己正逐渐发现，基本上没有过去、现在和未来，经由你们自己的心理时间实验，你们也会在我给你们其他资料之前，先直接体验到它。", "en": "You are discovering for yourself that basically there is no past, present and future, through your own experiments with psychological time, and you will also experience directly other material sometime before I have given it to you.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第54节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "54", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-023-e0327", "zh": "在我的环境中，没有下午四点或晚上九点。我这样说是指我不受时间顺序所限制。但也没有什么能阻止我去体验时间顺序，如果我如此选择的话。我们是按照经验的强度来感受“时间”，或类似时间的东西——一个“心理时间”。具有它自己的高峰与低谷。", "en": "There is no four o’clock in the afternoon or nine o’clock in the evening in my environment. By this I mean that I am not restricted to a time sequence. There is nothing preventing me from experiencing such sequences if I choose. We experience time, or what you would call its equivalent nature, in terms of intensities of experience — a psychological time with its own peaks and valleys.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第515节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "515", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0328", "zh": "当时间仿佛加快或减慢，是与你自己情绪性的感受有些相似的，但在一些重要的地方却有极大的不同。我们的“心理时间”若以环境来比喻，可以比之为房间的墙壁，但在我们的例子，墙壁会不断地改变颜色、尺寸、高度、深度与宽度。", "en": "This is somewhat similar to your own emotional feelings when time seems speeded up or slowed down, but it is vastly different in important ways. Our psychological time could be compared in terms of environment to the walls of a room, but in our case the walls would be constantly changing in color, size, height, depth and width.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第515节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "515", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B03", "title": "它是梦的场地", "note": "梦是赛斯用来确认心理时间存在的第一件证据。醒时独自一人的内在心理时间，和梦里体验到的时间感之间有明显的相似处——这显示醒时自己与睡时自己「真的只是一个自己，任何对它们的区分都是人为的」¹。\n\n梦里过了两天，身体不会老两岁：你在梦的架构中经历的好几个小时甚至好几天，并没有被身体记录下来，是在物理时间的伪装之外²；就算内我仍然与身体相连，在梦的架构中你却不受一些非常重要的身体效应束缚³。心理时间是一个与内在世界之间的自然连结物，在梦里经历了几天，年龄并不随物理时间相对变老，甚至清醒时也能在其中得到休息和更新⁴。\n\n对称的另一半是：梦世界的影像在心理时间当中会持续，在物理时间当中却不会持续——这也是梦世界看起来和其他世界不一致的原因⁵。而要先了解心理实相、心理时间、心理经验与梦的存在，你们才学得会运用很多能力，因为这些能力是在潜意识层、也就是内在感官上使用的⁶。\n\n梦本身就是「全然主观、只存在于心理时间架构中的经验」所形成的，可它造成的改变会真实落到肉体架构里⁷。再往前推：一开始整个地球在一种梦的世界里运作，时间可以加快或拉长，那是一种心理时间⁸。", "src": "早期课第1册第 23、24、31 节；早期课第2册第 49 节；早期课第4册第 193 节；梦、进化与价值完成第 887 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": "q-concept-023-e0004", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第23节"}, {"n": 2, "id": "q-concept-023-e0008", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第24节"}, {"n": 3, "id": "q-concept-023-e0009", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第24节"}, {"n": 4, "id": "q-concept-023-e0012", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第24节"}, {"n": 5, "id": "q-concept-023-e0025", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第31节"}, {"n": 6, "id": "q-concept-023-e0069", "label": "早期课第2册 · 第49节"}, {"n": 7, "id": "q-concept-023-e0284", "label": "早期课第4册 · 第193节"}, {"n": 8, "id": "q-concept-023-e0333", "label": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第887节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-023-e0004", "zh": "我确信你现在可以了解。经常在醒时状态体验到的这种独自一人的内在心理时间，和梦里体验到的时间感之间的相似处。这本来是为了要让你看到，醒时自己与睡时自己之间另外一个相似处。换句话说，用意是作为另一个证据，显示它们真的只是一个自己，任何对它们的区分都是人为的。", "en": "You will I am sure see the similarity now between this inner, alone sort of psychological time, experienced very often in waking hours, and the sense of time experienced in dreams. This is meant to show you but one more point of similarity between the waking and sleeping selves. In other words it is meant as another proof that they are indeed but one self, and that any divisions between them are artificial.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第23节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "23", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0008", "zh": "任何来自内在感官的这种通讯，都会存在你们的心理时间。我也说过这个心理时间，在睡眠以及意识安静时运作。现在，在梦中以及在梦的架构中，你有一种经历了很多小时、甚至好几天的感觉。这些你似乎在梦中经历的几天或几个小时，并没有被你们的身体所记录下来，并且是在你们物理时间的伪装之外。如果在一个梦里，比如说，你在这个梦架构内经历了两天的时间，你在身体上并没有变老两天。", "en": "Any such communications coming through the inner senses will exist in your psychological time. I have said also that this psychological time operates during sleep and during quiet times of consciousness. Now in dreams and in the dream framework you have the feeling of experiencing many hours, or even days. These days or hours that you seem to experience in dreams are not recorded by the physical body, and are outside of your physical time camouflage. If in a dream for example you experience within the framework two days, physically you do not age for these two days.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第24节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "24", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0009", "zh": "我相信，你们可以看到，这能带领我们到许多地方。一方面，心理时间在内在实相的这部分中如此重要，因此就算你的内我仍然与身体相连，但在梦的架构中，你却不受一些非常重要的身体效应束缚。现在，如同你的梦似乎让你卷入独立于你的钟表时间之外的持续时间（duration）里———对此我还有很多话要说——就你的内在视觉而言，你也能够获得“持续时间”的真实体验。", "en": "I am sure you see the many places that this can lead us. For one thing, psychological time is so much a part of inner reality that even though your inner self is still connected to the physical body, you are in the dream framework free of some very important physical effects. Now as your dreams seem to involve you in duration that is independent of your clock time, and I have much more to say here, so can you achieve the actual experience of duration as far as your inner visions are concerned.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第24节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "24", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0012", "zh": "相对来说，这将是一节短课。我想做一个说明：正如我刚才所说，心理时间是一个与内在世界之间的自然连结物。当你在梦状态时，虽然在心理时间的架构内经历了几天或几个小时，但是年龄没有随着物理时间相对变老，因为你在发展心理时间运用时，即使意识清醒，也能在心理时间的架构内得到休息和更新。这对你的精神和身体状况有帮助的程度令人惊奇，你会发现，这一方面增添了生命力，而另一方面对睡眠的需求会有所减少。", "en": "This is going to be a rather brief session comparatively. One note I wanted to make: As I have said, psychological time is a natural connective to the inner world. Though you experience days or hours within the framework of psychological time during the dream state, and yet do not age for a comparable amount of physical time, so as you develop in your use of psychological time you will be able to rest and be refreshed within the framework of psychological time while you are consciously awake. This will aid your mental and physical state to an amazing degree, and you will discover added vitality on the one hand, and a somewhat decreased need to sleep on the other.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第24节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "24", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-023-e0025", "zh": "举一个很简单的例子，想想看你们使用自己的能量创造出你们的梦世界。同样，你们也创造了你们所谓真实的伪装世界，唯一的差别是，梦世界的影像在心理时间当中虽然会持续，但在物理时间当中并不会持续。还有，信不信由你，你们的个体性在你们梦世界的创造上拥有更多的自由，而这也是梦世界为什么看起来和其他世界不一致的原因。", "en": "In a very simple example, consider that you yourself use your own energy to create your dream world. In this way also you create your so-called real camouflage world, the only difference being that the dream world images do not have duration in physical time although they have duration in psychological time. And believe it or not, actually your individuality has much more freedom in the creation of your dream world, and this is the reason why the dream world does not appear consistent to others.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第31节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "31", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0069", "zh": "我一直想要谈这件事，因为我可以向你们证明这个梦世界的存在，以及它的持续性，一直都在广阔的现在之内。你们必须先了解心理实相、心理时间、心理经验，还有梦存在，才能学会运用很多能力，因为在以上提过的所有面向中，你们是在潜意识层使用你们的能力，也就是你们的内在感官。", "en": "I have wanted to cover this because I can prove the existence of this dream world to you, and its continuity, always within the spacious present. You must understand psychological reality, psychological time, psychological experience, and the dream existence before you can learn to utilize many abilities, since in all the mentioned aspects, you use your abilities, that is your inner senses, on a subconscious level.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第49节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "49", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-023-e0284", "zh": "梦一样是由那些全然主观、只存在于心理时间架构中的经验所形成。因此主观的经验会在肉体架构里产生明确的改变，这些改变并不是由物质事件所造成，而是由发生在梦境里的事件所产生，而这个梦境里的事件在你们物质宇宙里并没有实相。", "en": "It is formed equally by those experiences which are purely subjective, and which exist only within the psychological time framework. The subjective experiences therefore result in definite changes within the physical body framework. These changes are not caused because of a physical event, but because of an event occurring within a dream condition which has no reality in your physical universe.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第193节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "193", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0333", "zh": "那么，在一开始，物种尚无它们现在所具的形体，它们有假形（pseudo forms）——如果你喜欢的话可称之为做梦的身体——而且它们在肉体上无法生殖。它们对时间的经验完全不同，在一开始，整个地球在一种梦的世界里运作。以你们的说法，这指时间可以加快或拉长。那是一种心理时间。", "en": "In the beginning, then, the species did not have the kinds of forms they do now. They had pseudoforms—dream bodies, if you prefer—and they could not physically reproduce themselves. Their experience of time was entirely different, and in the beginning the entire earth operated in a kind of dream time. In your terms, this meant that time could be quickened, or lengthened. It was a kind of psychological time.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第887节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "887", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B04", "title": "为什么它是「必经的通道」：伪装在这里松开", "note": "这一块讲的是机制，不是鼓励。不按他讲的方式应用心理时间，他就只能花好几页篇幅间接地用话语解释；而用上了，你们会立刻获得实相许多面向的第一手经验¹。甚至只是些微的学习，也会让你们对物质具备某些有价值的洞察力，因为它会为你们开启康庄大道²。\n\n目的是什么：有一个实相独立于你们的伪装模式之外，而他要你们不只是认识、还要能经验它——正确地运用心理时间是极为有用的帮助³；它或多或少也有助于你们探讨时空的本质⁴。\n\n最具体的机制在这里：当最大程度地利用心理时间时，伪装就几乎会变小到令人惊奇的程度⁵；而最依赖心理时间作用的那组内在感官，恰恰是涉及几近彻底解除伪装模式、不必采用另一套模式的那些，也最接近已揭露实相的直接体验⁶。它绕过的是物质法则——人格在很大程度上绕过了物质法则，更重要的是绕过某些通常会发生、并容易让物质架构负荷过重的化学反应⁷。\n\n所以研究与练习心理时间，会让你们看见内我的效力和实力，清楚看到它无论如何都不会完全受制于所谓的客观宇宙⁸。用他的话说：心理时间实验加强了你们在电子宇宙之内的机动性，在那里给你们「熟悉的地面，让你们在上面走、在上面旅行；参考地面，甚至是安全地面」⁹。", "src": "早期课第1册第 31、34 节；早期课第4册第 174 节；早期课第2册第 43、45、72 节；早期课第3册第 131 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": "q-concept-023-e0024", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第31节"}, {"n": 2, "id": "q-concept-023-e0023", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第31节"}, {"n": 3, "id": "q-concept-023-e0029", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第34节"}, {"n": 4, "id": "q-concept-023-e0274", "label": "早期课第4册 · 第174节"}, {"n": 5, "id": "q-concept-023-e0041", "label": "早期课第2册 · 第43节"}, {"n": 6, "id": "q-concept-023-e0045", "label": "早期课第2册 · 第43节"}, {"n": 7, "id": "q-concept-023-e0052", "label": "早期课第2册 · 第45节"}, {"n": 8, "id": "q-concept-023-e0124", "label": "早期课第2册 · 第72节"}, {"n": 9, "id": "q-concept-023-e0227", "label": "早期课第3册 · 第131节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-023-e0023", "zh": "演化定律在某方面是一种自我设限的定律，但也涉及到物质形成的必要原理。存有一直都在且永远都在，这个事实听起来之所以奇怪，甚至不可能，纯粹是你们目前视角的问题。不过，你们对心理时间的些微学习，甚至会让你们对物质具备某些有价值的洞察力，而且，心理时间的利用非常重要，因为它会为你们开启康庄大道。", "en": "The laws of evolution were self-limiting laws in one respect, but involve a necessary discipline in formation. The fact that entities always existed and always will exist sounds strange or even impossible simply because of your present perspective. Even your small studies with psychological time should give you some valuable insight into this matter, however, and the use of psychological time is very important because of the avenues which it will open for you.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第31节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "31", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0024", "zh": "假如你们能按照我所说的去应用心理时间，就会立刻获得实相中很多面向的第一手经验，我得花好几页的篇幅间接地使用话语来解释的面向。所有的存有，基本上都是能量或生命力的自我觉察（self-aware）的部分。他们是自生的（self generating），不可能以开始或结束的角度来理解。同样的，你们之所以认为一切事物都有开始和结束，只因为你们自己经验到的是伪装束缚资料(camouflage imprisoned data)的关系。", "en": "If you use psychological time as I have told you, you will get immediate firsthand experience of many facets of reality which take me pages to explain with the indirect use of words. All entities basically are self-aware portions of energy or vitality. They are self-generating and there is no possibility of thinking in terms of either beginning or end. Again, it is only your own camouflage- imprisoned data which makes you think that everything has a beginning and an end.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第31节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "31", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0029", "zh": "认识到你们特定的伪装模式是实相的一部分，是一回事；而要明白，有一个实相独立于你们的伪装模式之外，又是另一回事。我的目的之一是，是要让你们不仅能认识也能经验这个独立的实相，而且，再说一次，正确地运用心理时间是极为有用的帮助。", "en": "It is one thing to recognize that your particular camouflage patterns are part of reality and another to realize that there is a reality that is independent of your camouflage patterns. One of my purposes is to enable you not only to recognize but experience this independent reality, and again the use of psychological time in a correct manner will be an invaluable aid.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第34节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "34", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0274", "zh": "如同我提过的，心理时间的经验或多或少也有助于你们探讨时空的本质。", "en": "As I mentioned, your psychological time experiences will also help you to investigate the nature of time and space to some degree.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第174节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "174", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-023-e0041", "zh": "比如说，甚至在很大程度上，飘浮（levitation）也涉及到伪装，因为伪装身体本身向上升起，但我们在这里仍然使用伪装的身体形态。当然，没有伪装肉体形态的移动是巨大的一步，但它是可能的一步，这取决于你们的发展。但是这里你正在穿越伪装空间。在你目前的程度，不用任何伪装而要这么做非常困难，但是可以做得到；这里我再说一遍，使用心理时间是极为重要的，因为当最大程度地利用心理时间时，伪装就几乎会变小到令人惊奇的程度。", "en": "Even for example, levitation is involved with camouflage to a large degree, in that the camouflage physical body itself rises, but we are still here using the camouflage physical form. Traveling without the camouflage physical form is a giant step, of course, but a possible one according to your development. Here you are traveling however through camouflage space. It is very difficult on your level to do without any camouflage, and yet it can be done; and here again the use of psychological time is extremely important, since when psychological time is utilized to its fullest extent, then camouflage becomes lessened to an almost astounding degree.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第43节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "43", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0045", "zh": "我们现在关切的这组内在感官，处理的是一套伪装模式的解套，以及另一套的采用。最依赖心理时间作用的内在感官群组，就是涉及几近彻底解除伪装模式，不必采用其他模式的那些，而且这些也许是最重要的，因为它们比较接近已揭露实相的直接体验。", "en": "The grouping of inner senses with which we are now concerned deal with the disentanglement of one set of camouflage patterns and the taking up of another set. The groupings of inner senses most dependent upon the use of psychological time are those which involve a nearly complete disentanglement from camouflage pattern, without taking on other patterns, and these are perhaps the most important because they come closer to the direct experience of unveiled reality.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第43节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "43", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0052", "zh": "心理时间的运用对于任何实验都是基本的要件。这样运用心理时间是极其重要的，因为它使人格在很大程度上绕过了物质法则；而且还有更重要的是，绕过某些化学反应，那些反应通常会发生，而且也容易让物质架构负荷过重。", "en": "The use of psychological time is a basic necessity for any experiment. Such use of psychological time is extremely important, since it enables the personality to bypass physical laws to a large extent; and also, and this is important, bypass certain chemical reactions that would ordinarily occur, and tend to overtax the physical structure.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第45节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "45", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-023-e0124", "zh": "心理时间的研究和练习会让你们看见那个内我的效力和实力，如此一来，你们就会清楚看到它无论如何都不会完全受制于所谓的客观宇宙。物质并不是一个禁锢形式，它是意识在物质场域的限制之内，表现它自己的一种方式。", "en": "Study and practice with psychological time will show you the validity and strength of that inner self, so that you will clearly see that it is not completely bound to the so-called objective universe by any means. Matter is not an imprisoning form. It is a means by which consciousness expresses itself within the limits of the physical field.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第72节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "72", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0227", "zh": "在最近这些课里的资料，将是未来讨论的基础。我们更加深入实相的意义，以及实相的各个面向。我们目前的程序非常顺利，让我能够讨论一些对我们以前的方法而言太复杂的事情。在我们结束之前，我想要你们了解，你们的心理时间实验加强了你们在电子宇宙之内的机动性和潜意识的操纵。所有的心灵经验在这里一定有实相，也就是说，在电子系统里。没有任何心灵经验没有这样的电子实相。你们的心理实验在那里给你们熟悉的地面，让你们在上面走、在上面旅行；参考地面，甚至是安全地面。", "en": "The material in these last sessions will be basic for further discussions. We are going much deeper into the meaning of reality, and the aspects of reality. Our present procedure is working out very well, and it is enabling me to discuss matters that were too complicated for our earlier method. Before we close I want you to understand that your experiments in psychological time add to your mobility and subconscious manipulation within the electrical universe. And all psychic experience must have reality here, that is, within the electrical system. There is no psychic experience which does not have such electric reality. Your psychological experiments give you familiar ground there to walk upon, to travel on; grounds of reference and even of safety.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第131节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "131", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B05", "title": "转换焦点：它让你经验到本来经验不到的实相", "note": "这几段来自较后期的课，讲的是「转焦点」这件事本身。在心理时间里，当你们关闭惯常的感知方法时，你们能对别的方法有些体验——难点在于自我牢牢依附于对身体感官的使用¹。\n\n它能打开什么：你现在的行动可以同时影响未来的人格与过去的人格，光凭知性理解不了，必须伸展想象力去感觉，而「心理时间是你感知这些事实的最好方法」²。因为他要你看见的是——你们幻觉出这个房间，在此与在心理时间里一样都处于出神状态；如果此生是个出神状态，那你就能把意识的方向转去感知现在就存在的那些更大的实相，「你就坐在你自己的奇迹内却还在要求一个奇迹」³。\n\n说到底，正确地了解如何用心理时间，你就多少能学着改变意识的本质与焦点，把它自物质实相转开而贯注在其他方面——这不是说肉身会被丢下，而是你将开始探索自己的实相，以及你在其中存在的那些其他的实相⁴。所以他强调：他指的不只是冥想方法，而是你们主动去做的主观活动与探索⁵。", "src": "早期课第9册第 467 节；灵魂永生第 558、596 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": "q-concept-023-e0323", "label": "早期课第9册 · 第467节"}, {"n": 2, "id": "q-concept-023-e0329", "label": "灵魂永生 · 第558节"}, {"n": 3, "id": "q-concept-023-e0330", "label": "灵魂永生 · 第558节"}, {"n": 4, "id": "q-concept-023-e0331", "label": "灵魂永生 · 第596节"}, {"n": 5, "id": "q-concept-023-e0332", "label": "灵魂永生 · 第596节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-023-e0323", "zh": "因此，在心理时间里，至少是可能的：当你们关闭惯常的感知方法时，你们能对别的方法有些体验。然而自我却牢牢依附于对身体感官的使用。在梦境状态里，也至少能多少体验到别的一些方法", "en": "In psychological time therefore it is at least possible that you can have some experience with other methods when you close off habitual methods of perception. The ego is firmly attached to the use of the physical senses, however. In the dream state there can also be other methods at least slightly experienced", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第467节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "467", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0329", "zh": "同时，你现在的行动可以影响未来的人格，就如影响到过去的人格一样。你必须试着伸展你的想象力来感觉这些实相，因为光凭知性你无法理解，“心理时间”是你感知这些事实的最好方法。", "en": "Also, your actions now can affect the future personality as well as the past one. You must try to stretch your imagination and feel these realities, because the intellect alone cannot comprehend them. Psychological time is your best method for perceiving these actualities.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第558节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "558", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0330", "zh": "当我到这儿来说话的时候，我集中我的能量，但却不是朝着这房间，把它当作一个目的地，因为以你们的话来说这房间对我并不存在。以你们的话来说，这房间甚至对你们也不存在。你们假装同意它存在；我们并不在时间或空间的任何地点相会。发生于此地的真正相会，和这个房间或你们以为自己是的人并不相干。你们知道你们幻觉出这房间，在此你们与当你们在心理时间里一样，都是在出神状态里。我只是要你们了悟，如果此生是个出神状态，那么你就可以把你意识的方向转去感知现在就存在的那些更大的实相。你们能觉察你们自己更大的本体，就像我一样。你就坐在你自己的奇迹内却还在要求一个奇迹。我要打开的就是你的“心眼”。", "en": "When I come here to speak I focus my energy, but not toward this room as a destination, for in your terms this room does not exist to me. In your terms, this room does not even exist to you. You pretend to agree that it does; we meet in no place of space or time. The true meetings that take place here have nothing to do with the room or the people that you think you are. You know that you hallucinate the room, that you are as much in trance here as you ever are when you are in psychological time. I simply want you to realize that if this life is a trance, then you can turn the direction of your consciousness to perceive greater realities that presently exist. You can be aware of your own greater identity, even as I am. You sit within the miracle of yourselves and ask for signs. It is your inner eyes I would open.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第558节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "558", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-023-e0331", "zh": "现在：当你正确地了解如何用“心理时间”的时候，那么你就多少能学着改变你意识的本质与焦点。你能把它转向许多方向，你也能把它自物质实相转开而贯注在其他的方面。这并不指你的肉身会孤独无助地被留在此，它的真意是指你将开始探索你自己的实相，以及你在其中存在的那些其他的实相。", "en": "Now: When you properly understand how to use psychological time, then to some extent you can learn to alter the nature and focus of your consciousness. You can turn it in many directions. You can focus it in other ways, away from physical reality. This does not mean that you will be left high and dry here. It does mean that you will begin to explore the reality of yourselves, and of those other dimensions in which you have your existence.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第596节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "596", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0332", "zh": "你们对“心理时间”讨论了很多。我并不光是指我教的冥想方法。我的确是指你们主动去做的主观活动与探索。你们懂吗？我很高兴！", "en": "Now: There are many words for psychological time. I do not mean my method of meditation alone. I do mean subjective activity on your part, and exploration. Do you follow me? I am glad!", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第596节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "596", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B06", "title": "赛斯给的规矩，和用上了会怎样", "note": "目的先说全：适当利用心理时间，不仅会引领你到内在世界，还会防止你在物质世界里被催赶——在心理时间的架构内，你会发现一种安静沉着的平安¹；而当资讯出现时，你可以学着辨认、运用和控制它，在心理时间的架构内延长这种经验²。\n\n规矩琐碎但都算数：从 15 分钟开始、按提示进行³；每天固定时间、以 20 分钟为限，而且可能要经过两年才看得到明显的变化⁴；实验前用吸饱水的棉布敷在眼睑上最有用⁵；做的时候心中要有某个特定的事，否则「时间的成分会变得混乱」⁶；床头朝北时这项练习会做得很好⁷。但也别矫枉过正——并不是一找到几分钟空档就拿来做实验⁸。珍给自己下的暗示只有一条：完全放松，也摆脱了时间和空间的束缚⁹。\n\n用上了会怎样：每次练习，你就增强了自己的能力，虽然结果并不总是立竿见影¹⁰；熟练之后，在自动运用心理时间的辅助之下，你会运作得更有效率，也能轻松接受能量的支持¹¹；而最直接的回报是——在短短一段钟表时间内收到很大的充电和放松，对睡眠的需求减到最少¹²。", "src": "早期课第2册第 48、57、59、69、78、84 节；早期课第4册第 151、161、178 节；早期课第9册第 437 节；早期课第1册第 24、25、33、35 节；早期课第3册第 100、132 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": "q-concept-023-e0016", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第24节"}, {"n": 2, "id": "q-concept-023-e0019", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第24节"}, {"n": 3, "id": "q-concept-023-e0267", "label": "早期课第4册 · 第161节"}, {"n": 4, "id": "q-concept-023-e0251", "label": "早期课第4册 · 第151节"}, {"n": 5, "id": "q-concept-023-e0121", "label": "早期课第2册 · 第69节"}, {"n": 6, "id": "q-concept-023-e0315", "label": "早期课第9册 · 第437节"}, {"n": 7, "id": "q-concept-023-e0034", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第35节"}, {"n": 8, "id": "q-concept-023-e0231", "label": "早期课第3册 · 第132节"}, {"n": 9, "id": "q-concept-023-e0061", "label": "早期课第2册 · 第48节"}, {"n": 10, "id": "q-concept-023-e0106", "label": "早期课第2册 · 第59节"}, {"n": 11, "id": "q-concept-023-e0020", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第25节"}], "groups": [{"label": "怎么安排", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-023-e0121", "zh": "事实上，在做心理时间实验之前，用棉布吸饱水，敷在眼睑上最有用。用水洗眼睛，对你们两个都有帮助。有时候水温会低到45度。", "en": "In fact, cotton soaked in this water, and applied upon the eyelids before psychological time experiments would be the most beneficial. Bathing in the water, as you will of course, will help you both. At some times the temperature of the water will be as low as 58 degrees Fahrenheit.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第69节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "69", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0267", "zh": "我建议做心理时间练习，从15分钟开始，并按照约瑟所提示的说明进行。你们这时会发现与你们自己的某些部分非常亲密，而那些部分是你们容易忽略的，也是自我容易忽略的。你们确实会觉得更清晰、更放松。约瑟，我建议你这些说明更明确些，你可以做得比先前更好。", "en": "I would suggest for the psychological time experiments, fifteen minutes to begin with, along the lines of the directions which Joseph has given. You will find here an intimacy with portions of yourself which you would tend to ignore, which the ego would tend to ignore. You will find indeed refreshment and release. I would suggest that the directions, Joseph, be more specific. You can do better than you have done.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第161节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "161", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0315", "zh": "这些表征，我相信你会觉得适合你；其中一些资料应当能帮你解读你在心理时间里收到的信息。不过在这些情形里，你心中应当有某个特定的事。否则时间的成分会变得混乱。", "en": "Now these symbols are those that I believe you will find suitable for you, and some of the information should help you interpret information received in psychological time. In these instances however you should have something particular in mind. Otherwise the time element can become confused.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第437节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "437", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0034", "zh": "后面的房间是睡觉最好的地方。不过，约瑟，它也是你工作的最佳选择。这个小房间可以用来当卧室，但是床头应该朝向北方。要是你们的头朝北，在使用心理时间练习时，你们会做得很好。", "en": "The back room is the best for sleeping. However it is also the best for your working purposes, Joseph. The small room will do as a sleeping room, but the head of the bed should be at the north. And in the use of psychological time exercises you would do well if your head was at the north.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第35节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "35", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0164", "zh": "你们一直享有的非正式社交活动非常有益，在合理的范围内应该继续。床位的改变也有助于在那里进行的心理时间实验。", "en": "The informal social engagements that you have been enjoying are most beneficial, and within reason should be continued. The change in the direction of the bed will also aid in psychological time experiments, when tried there.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第100节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "100", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0231", "zh": "从向外集中的焦点完全变成向内集中的焦点，很有助益，但这并不是说，每次一找到几分钟空档就要拿来做心理时间实验。不管怎样，轻快的散步应该是鲁柏每天都要做的事，而且散步也可以提振内我。", "en": "A complete change from intense focus outward to intense focus inward is most beneficial, but this does not mean that every few minutes found available be spent in psychological time experiments. Brisk walks should be a daily part of Ruburt's schedule in any case, and walking also refreshes the inner self.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第132节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "132", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0251", "zh": "这里加一个注：鲁柏可以试着每天做20分钟的心理时间练习；而且应该每天固定时间练习。我现在会建议他认真开始把这件事排进日常活动时间表当中。约瑟，你最好和他一起待在家里。事实上，由于你们自己的修为，在我所谓的短时间内，你们的生活将会舒适得多；但是对你们来说，可能要经过两年，才看得到明显的变化。", "en": "A note here: Ruburt may try the psychological time experiments twenty minutes daily; and indeed yes, the time of the day should be uniform. I would suggest now that he seriously begin to schedule this with his daily activities. It is best that you be in the house with him, Joseph. And indeed, for your own edification your life in general will be much more comfortable within what I would call a short time; though to you this may be two years, before a noticeable change is apparent.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第151节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "151", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0028", "zh": "约瑟，你应该继续你自己的心理时间实验，因为在这些课当中，我们也依赖于你的能力。", "en": "You should continue your own experiments in the use of psychological time, Joseph, as we also depend upon your abilities in these sessions.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第33节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "33", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0099", "zh": "你们接收到宝贵的资料，特别是最近。当然要继续做你们的心理时间实验。", "en": "You have been receiving valuable information, particularly of late. Of course continue with your psychological time experiments.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第57节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "57", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0139", "zh": "心理时间的实验应该要再度进行了，依你们的进展按照上面的说明做些改变。", "en": "They should be taken up again, and alternated with the above directions, according to your development.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第78节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "78", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0144", "zh": "我再次建议你们找时间重读前面的资料，并且把心理时间实验排进每天的日程中。", "en": "I suggest again that you reread some of our earlier material when you find time, and that you resume your psychological time experiments in some kind of schedule.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第84节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "84", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "用上了会怎样", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-023-e0020", "zh": "如果你们用我说过的方法使用心理时间，会发现我已经给了你们一个一个时间的礼物，因为你会在短短的一段钟表时间内收到很大的充电和放松。你对睡眠的需求会减到最少，这涉及你那方的某种训练，但那训练是相当容易的，应该不会太困难。", "en": "If you use psychological time in the manner which I described, you will find that I have given you a time gift, in that you will receive great refreshment and relaxation in a short period of clock time. And your need for sleep will be minimized. This involves some training on your part, but is relatively easy and should come without too much difficulty.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第25节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "25", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0061", "zh": "每次练习使用心理时间的时候，你就增强了你自己的能力，虽然结果可能并不总是立竿见影。这里牵涉到制约，其他任何一件事情都是如此，不过这代表你到当前为止达到的最高点，我敢肯定，你会进步。在这方面你展现了很强的能力，也有做实验的内在意愿，这将使你处于非常有利的地位。", "en": "Each time you practice with the use of psychological time, you add to your abilities, though results may not always be immediate. There is conditioning involved here, as with anything else, but this represents one of your very highest points so far, and I am certain that you will improve. You show a good deal of ability along this line, and possess an inner willingness to experiment, that will stand you in very good stead.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第48节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "48", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0106", "zh": "一个太过有意识的行动是没有帮助的，但这份资料应该有帮助。物质有机体确实需要睡眠，但只有带着脑子的物质有机体需要睡眠。心智一直保持警觉。但是当你们愈来愈熟练时，在自动运用心理时间的辅助之下，你们就能够运作得更有效率多了，也能够轻松接受能量的支持。", "en": "Too-conscious an attempt will not help, but this material should help. The physical organism does indeed require sleep, but only the physical organism with its brain. The mind is continually in vigilance. Nevertheless when you are more proficient you will, with the aid of automatic use of psychological time, be able to operate much more effectively, and be upheld by energy without strain.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第59节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "59", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0016", "zh": "当物理时间被一个安静的“我”追随和注视时，心理时间似乎流动得如此容易的原因就在这里。一个通往另一个，伪装是如此松散，足以让内在形式透射出来。适当利用心理时间，不仅会引领你到内在世界，还会防止你在物质世界里被催赶。在心理时间的架构内，你会发现一种安静沉着的平安。我跟你们两个讲这件事，是为了你们好，因为运用这些附加好处的收获很多。", "en": "This is why psychological time seems to flow so easily when physical time is pursued and watched by a quiet “I”. The one leads to the other and the camouflage is loose enough to let the inner form shine through. A proper use of psychological time will not only lead you into the inner world, but will also prevent you from being rushed in the physical world. Within it, that is within the framework of psychological time, you will discover a quiet and cool peacefulness. I tell you both this for your benefit, because both of you will gain much in the utilization of these added benefits.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第24节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "24", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0019", "zh": "如果你们能记住这一点的话，内在资讯将更容易传过来，你也会有能力控制它。它本身从来不会强烈到无法控制。有些能力你可以训练自己，像是当资讯出现时辨认、运用和控制它们。这也意味着就持续时间而言，你们可以运用它到某种程度。也就是说，在心理时间的架构内，你可以延长这种经验。", "en": "If you will remember this, inner data will come through much more easily, and you will be able to control it. It is never of itself overpowering. There are abilities in which you can train yourself, in both recognition of data when it occurs, utilization, and control. This also implies to some degree utilization as far as duration is concerned. That is, within the framework of psychological time you can lengthen such experiences.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第24节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "24", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B07", "title": "最常见的失败方式是用力：赛斯几次踩刹车", "note": "这一整块几乎是刹车记录，值得当成一节连着读。他反复出现的诊断只有一个：用力。「鲁柏最近在做心理时间练习时候太卖力了，他用意识心的做法，试图要他的潜意识运作和聚焦」¹；把它说成机制就是——「尝试得太过辛苦。这会造成压缩，我们要的是扩展」²。\n\n所以规矩得反过来写：千万不要有「不做就会完蛋」的态度，允许自己的心四处游走才有最佳表现，关闭自己的心就不会有效果——而鲁柏最近正是靠意志力聚精会神地练，自己并不知道³。做练习时要记得：往外聚焦的同时，其实也是在往内扩展与聚焦，必须先求扩展，才能获得扩展的成效⁴。\n\n处方是什么？「一种情感上的接纳就是答案」——成效不显著，很大一部分原因在于用太多意识专注在这件事上⁵；心灵体验的自发性不能给它太大压力，心理时间里的初步实验只是第一阶段⁶。而纪律过而不及，反而会妨碍本来很强的直觉，所以一定要缩减，内在的自发必须恢复⁷。\n\n什么时候该停：该休息时就忘掉实验，下周再做⁸；过度投入时实验也该暂停——如果意识心能转移注意力，直觉能力就会尽其本分开始运作⁹。别走太远、太快：他警告珍别太投入那种「狂喜」的经验¹⁰，也说在上一次实验之后就试图提醒她要小心谨慎¹¹。罗补记了第 54 节那条警告的后续：这种内在能量的集中如果发生在别人身上、被不知不觉地引导，可能会有令人不愉快的作用¹²。", "src": "早期课第2册第 54、69、78 节；早期课第4册第 178、186 节；早期课第3册第 100、102、130、140 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": "q-concept-023-e0120", "label": "早期课第2册 · 第69节"}, {"n": 2, "id": "q-concept-023-e0277", "label": "早期课第4册 · 第178节"}, {"n": 3, "id": "q-concept-023-e0278", "label": "早期课第4册 · 第178节"}, {"n": 4, "id": "q-concept-023-e0279", "label": "早期课第4册 · 第178节"}, {"n": 5, "id": "q-concept-023-e0135", "label": "早期课第2册 · 第78节"}, {"n": 6, "id": "q-concept-023-e0138", "label": "早期课第2册 · 第78节"}, {"n": 7, "id": "q-concept-023-e0168", "label": "早期课第3册 · 第102节"}, {"n": 8, "id": "q-concept-023-e0225", "label": "早期课第3册 · 第130节"}, {"n": 9, "id": "q-concept-023-e0282", "label": "早期课第4册 · 第186节"}, {"n": 10, "id": "q-concept-023-e0091", "label": "早期课第2册 · 第54节"}, {"n": 11, "id": "q-concept-023-e0240", "label": "早期课第3册 · 第140节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-023-e0120", "zh": "可以，虽然我想让你们发展自己的能力。鲁柏最近在做心理时间练习时候太卖力了，他用意识心的做法，试图要他的潜意识运作和聚焦。", "en": "Yes, although I want you to develop your own abilities. Ruburt has been trying too hard lately with psychological time, and trying to make his subconscious function and focus, in the same manner that the conscious mind does.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第69节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "69", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0277", "zh": "他在我们的课当中，做得相当好。不过他在心理时间的练习上，尝试得太过辛苦。这会造成压缩，我们要的是扩展。", "en": "He is doing very well in our sessions. However in his psychological time experiments he is trying too hard. This leads to a constriction. We want an expansion.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第178节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "178", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0278", "zh": "他千万不要有不做就会完蛋的态度，若能允许自己的心四处游走，就会有最佳表现，但若关闭自己的心，就不会有效果。最近他进行心理时间实验时，都是靠自己的意志力聚精会神地练习，不过他自己并不知道这一点，而这种做法会导致压缩。", "en": "He must avoid a do-or-die attitude. He does best when he allows his mind to wander, and not when he hems it in. In his psychological time experiments lately, he has concentrated with his will, though he did not realize he was doing so. Again, this leads to a constriction.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第178节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "178", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0279", "zh": "这里有很多细节我们还会详细讨论。但是他做心理时间练习时必须记得，不管是在宇宙里面或是穿透宇宙，他在往外聚焦的同时，其实也是在往内扩展与聚焦。他必须先求扩展，才能获得扩展的结果或成效。", "en": "There are many details here that we shall discuss most thoroughly. He must remember however in his psychological time experiments that to focus outward, within and through the universe, is to expand and focus inward simultaneously. He must seek the expansion before he seeks the results or effects of the expansion.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第178节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "178", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-023-e0135", "zh": "你们现在也正在做这件事。鲁柏现在正在这么做。你最近做心理时间的成效不显著，很大一部分原因出于你用太多意识专注在这件事情上。一种情感上的接纳就是答案，这一点在鲁柏听来也许不以为然，再说一次，在无限广阔的现在和大自然里的一次感官上的沉浸，将使你们焕然一新。", "en": "You are doing so now. Ruburt is doing so now. Your lack of success lately with psychological time has been to a large measure caused by too great a conscious concentration upon the task. An emotional acceptance, distasteful as this may seem to Ruburt, is the answer here, and again a sensual immersion in the spacious present and in nature will refresh you here.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第78节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "78", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0138", "zh": "心灵体验的自发性不能给它太大的压力，你们照着我给你们的这些方式去做，就会再度找到它。它们代表了第二阶段，而在心理时间里的初步实验代表第一阶段。", "en": "The spontaneity of psychic experience cannot be stressed too strongly, and you will find it again following these directions I have given you. They represent the second step, as the initial experiments in psychological time represented the first.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第78节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "78", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0168", "zh": "鲁柏一直在寻找纪律。他永远在寻找他缺少的纪律。他的直觉向来非常强。唉，现在他有他的纪律，但是过而不及，反而妨碍了非常强的直觉，所以一定要缩减。自发，内在的自发一定要恢复。他现在的心理时间实验比较上手了，他一定要让这种自发扩展到生命中的其他面向。鲁柏一定要全心全意地效力于这些课，它们的广度才会变大。", "en": "Ruburt has been in search of discipline. He was always in search of the discipline he lacked. His intuitions were always very strong. Well, now he has his discipline, but it has been overdone. It has come to hamper the very strong intuitions, and it must be lessened. Spontaneity, inner spontaneity must be restored. He is now doing better with his psychological time experiments, and he must let this spontaneity expand into other aspects of his life. Ruburt must be fully committed to these sessions for them to accelerate in scope.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第102节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "102", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0282", "zh": "心理时间的实验也该暂停。如果意识心能转移注意力，直觉能力就会尽其本分开始运作了。约瑟，你教他自律的这一部分做得很好，不过因为他做事从来就不会半途而废，所以有时候学东西会过度认真。这里还有一个重点：你自己的工作节奏跟他不一样。", "en": "The psychological-time experiments should also be suspended. When the conscious mind is so diverted the intuitions can do their work. You did well Joseph, teaching him discipline, but as he never goes halfway, so sometimes he learns his lessons too well. One point here also: you pace yourselves differently in your work.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第186节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "186", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "什么时候该停", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-023-e0225", "zh": "半出神状态并不允许你在任何一个世界里有清晰的觉察力。它通常很快就过了，同时在进入出神中途，也在回神的中途。它当然是两个实相的一部分，这不用说也知道。今晚有很多东西真的可以加进我们之前的讨论里，但是鲁柏，尤其是在昨晩的课之后，应该要休息。我也会建议他忘掉心理时间实验，下周一再做。", "en": "The semitrance state does not allow a clear awareness in either world. It is passed through very quickly as a rule, both on the way into a trance and on the way out of one. It is of course a part of both realities. This goes without saying. It is true that there is much this evening that could be added to our previous discussions, but Ruburt, particularly after last nights session, should rest. And I would also suggest that he forget his psychological time experiments until next Monday.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第130节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "130", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "别走太远、太快", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-023-e0091", "zh": "顺便说一句，我的确建议鲁柏在最近几天找个时间去看一下卡拉汉小姐。另外，重新读一下你们自己心理时间的实验记录。此外，我还要建议鲁柏别太投入他喜欢称为狂喜的经验，因为我们不想要他走太远，太快。", "en": "Incidentally, I do suggest that Ruburt make a short visit to Miss Callahan within the next few days. Also, reread your own accounts of your psychological time experiments. Also I would suggest that Ruburt go easy with what he prefers to call the experience of ecstasy, as we do not want him to go too far, too fast.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第54节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "54", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0240", "zh": "就在他上一次的心理时间实验之后，我的确试图告诉他要小心谨慎。当然啦，你们是有必要透过直接经验来学习；如果你，鲁柏，没有体验过一些，那么我警告你小心各种不舒服的效应，意义就不是那么大了。", "en": "I did indeed attempt to tell him to use caution, immediately after his last psychological time experiment. It is, of course, necessary that you learn through direct experience; and my warning you against various uncomfortable effects would not mean nearly as much if you did not, Ruburt, experience a few of them.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第140节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "140", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B08", "title": "它通向的地方：死亡、另一个自己、更大的实相", "note": "这几段散在各册，方向一致。关于死亡最直接的说明在这里：死亡一开始的感觉就像心理时间——在全然的自由进来之前，有一段时期你还守着伪装时间的概念，熟悉状况之前有一小段空隙¹；而心理时间的运用会让死亡的经验不那么可怕，因为到时你们已经学会认清什么是广阔的现在，意识自我不会因为突如其来的感知而那么不知所措²。\n\n它通向的也不只是死后：它们行经心理时间，在你们对它们的觉知消失之后继续存在——你们只是焦点不在那儿³。把这一块与「片刻点」接上会更清楚：人的一生寿命不过是一个片刻点，而你在物理时间的几个物理时刻之内获得的经验，完全独立于你们的时间结构之外⁴。\n\n回到此生，它解开的是「不够用」的焦虑：心理时间会把你放开，让你在所认识的时间里感受到价值完成与耐久——不要带着遗憾去想「你只有下午可以作画」，那会从两方面限制你⁵。\n\n它也改变你和自己的资料之间的关系：独自在心理时间实验里工作时，你就不那么害怕潜意识的浮现，也更信任自己的资料⁶——不像写作时那样，得担心某个「人物」是不是潜意识的虚构⁷。\n\n再往外一步：内我里还有另一个更为先进的部分。在心理时间里静下来，把你的物质宇宙和他的想象成两间房、中间有一条通道，告诉自己你愿意穿过去，他会在那里帮你做到⁸；用上心理时间的架构，这些有些可以是有意识的，你应该能相当清楚地看见他⁹。", "src": "早期课第2册第 48 节；早期课第3册第 115 节；早期课第6册第 269 节；早期课第9册第 456、466、486 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": "q-concept-023-e0063", "label": "早期课第2册 · 第48节"}, {"n": 2, "id": "q-concept-023-e0064", "label": "早期课第2册 · 第48节"}, {"n": 3, "id": "q-concept-023-e0210", "label": "早期课第3册 · 第115节"}, {"n": 4, "id": "q-concept-023-e0311", "label": "早期课第6册 · 第269节"}, {"n": 5, "id": "q-concept-023-e0318", "label": "早期课第9册 · 第456节"}, {"n": 6, "id": "q-concept-023-e0321", "label": "早期课第9册 · 第466节"}, {"n": 7, "id": "q-concept-023-e0322", "label": "早期课第9册 · 第466节"}, {"n": 8, "id": "q-concept-023-e0324", "label": "早期课第9册 · 第486节"}, {"n": 9, "id": "q-concept-023-e0325", "label": "早期课第9册 · 第486节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-023-e0063", "zh": "死亡，一开始的感觉就像心理时间。在全然的自由进来之前，有一段时期你还守着伪装时间的概念，而且熟悉状况之前有一小段空隙。", "en": "Death, at first, feels like psychological time. There is a period when you retain the idea of camouflage time, before full freedom enters in, and a small lapse before orientation is possible.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第48节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "48", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0064", "zh": "心理时间的运用将使死亡的经验不那么可怕。到时候，你们已经学会认清什么是广阔的现在，而意识自我也不会因为突如其来的感知而那么不知所措和困惑不安。", "en": "The use of psychological time will make the experience of death much less frightening. You will already have learned to recognize the spacious present for what it is, and the conscious ego will not be so bewildered and confused by the sudden perception that is involved.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第48节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "48", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0210", "zh": "它们行经心理时间。在你们对它们的觉知消失之后，它们继续存在。就因为你们的焦点——", "en": "They move through psychological time. Their existence continues after your awareness of them has vanished. Just because you focus—", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第115节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "115", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0311", "zh": "人的一生寿命不过是一个片刻点而已。自我是你能够用来探索和体验这个片刻点的那个部分。(微笑）价值完成需要感知的这种减速。这很难解释。想想心理时间的运用。你在物理时间的几个物理时刻之内获得经验，这些经验完全独立于你们的时间结构之外。", "en": "The span of a whole man’s lifetime is no more than a moment point. The ego is the portion of you equipped to explore and experience this moment point in depth. （Smile.） Value fulfillment demands this slowing down of perception. This is most difficult to explain. Consider using psychological time. You have experiences within a few physical moments of physical time, experiences that are entirely independent of your time structure.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第269节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "269", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0318", "zh": "你不必死命灌输。要紧的是那份感受。把自己看成在创造力上灵活的人。心理时间——你若细加思量——会把你放开，让你在你所认识的时间里感受到价值完成与耐久。不要带着遗憾去想：你只有下午可以作画。这会从两个主要方面限制你。", "en": "You need not hammer this. The feeling is what is important. Think of yourself as being flexible creatively. Psychological time, if you contemplate it, will set you free, so that you feel value fulfillment and durability within the time that you know. Do not think in terms regretfully that you have only afternoons in which to work. This restricts you in two main ways.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第456节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "456", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-023-e0321", "zh": "当你独自在心理时间的实验里工作时，你就不那么害怕潜意识的浮现，你也更信任你的资料。你觉得那些体验至少是你自己的，不像你的写作时那样，非得有个贝加[Bega]（苏马利语）要借你说话。", "en": "When you are working alone in psychological time experiments, you do not so fear emergence of the subconscious, and you trust your material more. You feel that the experiences are at least your own, with no Bega who must speak through you as in your writings.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第466节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "466", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0322", "zh": "我的意思只是，在那些写作课里，你有时仍然担心，那位人物究竟是不是潜意识的虚构；但在你的心理时间实验里，你对这一点的感觉就没有那么强烈，因为那些实验提供了属于你自己的心智活动。", "en": "I simply meant that at times you still worried as to whether or not he was a subconscious fiction in the writing sessions; but you did not feel this as strongly in your psychological-time experiments, because of the mental activity of your own that they provided.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第466节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "466", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0324", "zh": "你们整个内我里还有另一个部分，另一个更为先进的部分。我先前提到过，在一个可能系统里，你们是一位把绘画当作业余爱好的医生。他的名字是皮特拉[PIETRA]（逐字拼读）。在心理时间里，或者单单在你们静下来的时候，闭上眼，把你们的物质宇宙想象成我们比喻中的一间房间，把他的想象成另一间，两者之间有一条通道。告诉你自己，你愿意穿过那条通道旅行，而他会在那里帮你做到。", "en": "There is another portion of your whole inner self, another more advanced. I mentioned earlier that in one probability system you were a doctor who painted as a hobby. His name is P I E T R A. (Spelled out.) In psychological time or simply when you are still, close your eyes and imagine your physical universe as one room in our analogy, and his as another with a passageway between. Tell yourself that you would like to travel through that passageway, and that he will be there to help you do so.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第486节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "486", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0325", "zh": "我重复一遍：如果你们用上一个心理时间的架构，这其中有些可以是有意识的。你们应该能相当清楚地看见他。在他的实相里，他正着手一系列实验，这些实验会把他引到你们这里来——前提是他进展得当。", "en": "I repeat: some of this can be conscious, if you use a psychological-time framework. You should be able to see him rather clearly. In his reality he is embarking upon a series of experiments that will lead him to you, if he proceeds properly.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第486节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "486", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B10", "title": "它站在哪些概念中间：内在时间感、品质-深度、观念感官", "note": "赛斯自己也在给这个词找位置。他把心理时间放进更大的谱系：它是「我目前暂时称为内在时间感的一部分」¹；而且早在人类以特定伪装模式建构起来之前，人类的自我意识就已存在于心理时间和内在时间里——换句话说，打从物质宇宙一开始，人类意识天生就潜伏着了²。\n\n相邻的一个坐标是「品质-深度」：那种透过品质或价值维度采取的行动，「大可以被称为你们心理时间的内在延伸」³。他甚至说心理时间像一层外缘，涉及你们最初的冒险行动，而品质-深度才是唯一真实的前景，不涉及任何间隔⁴；继续进行心理时间实验，你们和它的关联就会愈来愈多⁵。\n\n再往观念那一侧接：借由心理时间的使用，你们能以最佳方式达到接近「直接经验观念」的程度⁶。罗在注释里把这条接回第四个内在感官——观念感官：有些东西你不可能真正明白，除非你变成它们，而「你可以达到最接近这个想法的，是利用心理时间」⁷。", "src": "早期课第1册第 26、37 节；早期课第2册第 59 节；早期课第5册第 204 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": "q-concept-023-e0021", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第26节"}, {"n": 2, "id": "q-concept-023-e0022", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第26节"}, {"n": 3, "id": "q-concept-023-e0103", "label": "早期课第2册 · 第59节"}, {"n": 4, "id": "q-concept-023-e0104", "label": "早期课第2册 · 第59节"}, {"n": 5, "id": "q-concept-023-e0105", "label": "早期课第2册 · 第59节"}, {"n": 6, "id": "q-concept-023-e0036", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第37节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-023-e0021", "zh": "这一切都涉及一个观念，我不太愿意说是进步，而是一种沿着特定方向改变的观念。我们讲过精神基因，这些或多或少是物质的心灵蓝图，在这些精神基因里，存在着你们人类那种自我意识的模式。不过，它看起来并没有建构好，也就是说有建构好的形式，过了很长一段物理时间，而且我们讨论过心理时间是我目前暂时称为内在时间感(inner time sense)的一部分。", "en": "All this involved an idea of, and I hesitate to say advancement, but an idea of change along certain lines. We have spoken of mental genes. These are more or less psychic blueprints for physical matter, and in these mental genes existed the pattern for your human type of self-consciousness. It did not appear constructed, that is in constructed form, for a long period of physical time however, and we have discussed psychological time as being part of what I will call for now an inner time sense.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第26节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "26", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0022", "zh": "早在你们人类以特定的伪装模式建构它之前，人类的自我意识就已经存在心理时间和内在时间里。为了你们的朋友，我把这一点简化一下：打从你们物质宇宙一开始，人类意识天生就潜伏着了。", "en": "This human self-consciousness existed in psychological time and in inner time long before you as a species constructed it in terms of your particular camouflage patterns. For your friend’s sake I will simplify this, saying that human consciousness was inherent and latent from the beginning of your physical universe.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第26节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "26", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0036", "zh": "你们直接经验观念就会发现这个，而且借由心理时间的使用，你们能以最佳方式达到某些接近完成的程度。所谓体验观念，无疑就是从头到尾跟随这个观念。亲爱的，既没有开始也没有结束，你们的这种观念是全然又彻底专注在伪装时间的结果。", "en": "You will discover this by experiencing the idea directly, and you can best achieve some approximation of accomplishment by using psychological time. Your idea of experiencing a concept is doubtlessly to follow it through from beginning to end. Sweet tootsies, there is no beginning or end, and this idea of yours is the result of a complete and utter concentration upon camouflage time.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第37节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "37", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0103", "zh": "但是在一个出神的深度里，就像在品质-深度中，运动有它的方向，但不能想成东西、南北、上下。这个运动是一个透过品质或价值维度采取的行动。我一直想谈这一点。它大可以被称为你们心理时间的内在延伸，这么说你们就会知道它的重要性了。", "en": "But in a trance depth, as in Quality-depth, the motion has a direction that cannot be thought of in terms of up or down, north or south, east or west. The motion is action through quality or value dimension. I have been meaning to speak about this. It could easily be called the inner extension of your psychological time, so you will see its importance.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第59节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "59", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0104", "zh": "心理时间确实涉及你们最初的冒险行动。它像一层外缘。这品质-深度是我们唯一真实的前景。再说一次，不涉及任何间隔。我发现难以为我的意思找到具有启发性的字词。", "en": "Psychological time indeed involves you in the initial venturing. It is like an outer rim. This Quality-depth is our only true perspective. Again, no intervals are involved. I find difficulty in choosing words evocative for my meaning.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第59节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "59", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-023-e0105", "zh": "你们很可能猜到了，品质-深度可以加进我们的内在宇宙法则或原则里。继续进行你们的心理时间实验，你们和它的关联就会愈来愈多。", "en": "Quality-depth, as you probably guessed, can be added to our rules or principles of the inner universe. You will have more to do with it as your experiments with psychological time continue.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第59节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "59", "only_en": false}]}]}], "reading": [], "books": [{"name": "早期课第1册", "count": 27}, {"name": "早期课第2册", "count": 23}, {"name": "早期课第4册", "count": 8}, {"name": "早期课第3册", "count": 7}, {"name": "早期课第9册", "count": 7}, {"name": "灵魂永生", "count": 6}, {"name": "梦、进化与价值完成", "count": 1}, {"name": "早期课第6册", "count": 1}], "span": [1963, 1979], "stats": {"blocks": 9, "quotes": 80, "reading": 0, "reading_tagged": 0, "tagged": 0, "only_en": 0}};
